/-
# Free points outside the rhombus (Kourovka Notebook Problem 4.41)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.41 (Yu. I. Merzlyakov): a point `z` in the
complex plane is called free if the matrices `[[1, 2], [0, 1]]` and `[[1, 0], [z, 1]]` generate a
free group. Are all points outside the rhombus with vertices `±2`, `±i` free?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Basic.Complex.Basic
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreePointsOutsideRhombusKourovka4Problem41Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.41 (Yu. I.
Merzlyakov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700249 (`KOU-4.41`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The matrices are taken in `SL₂(ℂ)`. For `z ≠ 0` they do not commute, so they generate a free group
exactly when they freely generate a free group of rank `2` (a `2`-generated non-abelian free group
is free on any generating pair, being Hopfian); "free" is stated as injectivity of `F₂ → SL₂(ℂ)`.
Outside the closed rhombus means `|Re z| / 2 + |Im z| > 1`.
-/

/-- The matrix `[[1, 2], [0, 1]]` in `SL₂(ℂ)`. -/
def upperMatrix : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℂ :=
  ⟨!![1, 2; 0, 1], by simp [Matrix.det_fin_two]⟩

/-- The matrix `[[1, 0], [z, 1]]` in `SL₂(ℂ)`. -/
def lowerMatrix (z : ℂ) : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℂ :=
  ⟨!![1, 0; z, 1], by simp [Matrix.det_fin_two]⟩

/-- `z` is a free point: `[[1, 2], [0, 1]]` and `[[1, 0], [z, 1]]` generate a free group of rank
`2`, freely: the homomorphism from the free group on two generators sending them to the two
matrices is injective. -/
def IsFreePoint (z : ℂ) : Prop :=
  Function.Injective (FreeGroup.lift ![upperMatrix, lowerMatrix z])

/-- Kourovka 4.41 (Yu. I. Merzlyakov): every point `z` outside the closed rhombus with vertices
`±2`, `±i` (that is, with `|Re z| / 2 + |Im z| > 1`) is free. -/
def pointsOutsideRhombusFree : Prop :=
  ∀ z : ℂ, 1 < |z.re| / 2 + |z.im| → IsFreePoint z

/--
Resolved false: Ignatov and Shkuratskiĭ found points `z` outside the rhombus with vertices `±2`,
`±i` for which `[[1, 2], [0, 1]]` and `[[1, 0], [z, 1]]` do not generate a free group; the Kourovka
Archive answers 4.41 "No". Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in
Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved
Problems, Problem 4.41 (Yu. I. Merzlyakov); resolution: Yu. A. Ignatov, Free and nonfree subgroups
of PSL₂(C) generated by two parabolic elements, Math. USSR-Sb. 35 (1979), 49-55; A. I. Shkuratskiĭ,
Math. Notes 24 (1978), 720-721, Kourovka Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.41: No,
https://doi.org/10.1070/SM1979v035n01ABEH001449.
-/
public theorem_wanted pointsOutsideRhombusFree_refuted : ¬ pointsOutsideRhombusFree

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreePointsOutsideRhombusKourovka4Problem41Wanted
